# 🛒 mPointShop-Rework

> End-to-end UI and API test automation framework for the mPointShop platform — built with Python, Selenium, and pytest.

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.12-3776AB?style=flat&logo=python&logoColor=white)
![Selenium](https://img.shields.io/badge/Selenium-4.x-43B02A?style=flat&logo=selenium&logoColor=white)
![pytest](https://img.shields.io/badge/pytest-8.x-0A9EDC?style=flat&logo=pytest&logoColor=white)
![Allure](https://img.shields.io/badge/Allure-Report-orange?style=flat)
![Requests](https://img.shields.io/badge/Requests-API_Testing-red?style=flat)

---

## 📌 Overview

This project demonstrates real-world QA automation practices including structured test design, Page Object Model architecture, environment configuration, and stable synchronization strategies.

It covers both **UI (E2E) testing** via Selenium and **API testing** via Requests — with full Allure reporting and automatic failure artifact collection.

---

## ⚙️ Tech Stack

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python 3.12 | Language |
| Selenium | Browser automation |
| pytest | Test runner |
| Requests | API testing |
| Allure | Test reporting |
| Faker | Dynamic test data generation |
| python-dotenv | Environment variable management |
| pytest-xdist | Parallel test execution |
| pytest-repeat | Repeat tests for stability checks |

---

## 🗂️ Project Structure

```
mPointShop-Rework/
│
├── api/
│   ├── endpoints/
│   │   └── auth_api.py             # Auth endpoint methods
│   └── client.py                   # Base API client (session, headers, base URL)
│
├── config/
│   └── env_config.py               # Environment config (no secrets)
├── pages/                          # Page Object Model classes
├── drivers/                        # WebDriver setup
├── fixtures/                       # Reusable pytest fixtures
├── utils/                          # Helpers & utilities
├── data/                           # Test data & builders
│
├── tests/
│   ├── e2e/                        # UI tests (Selenium)
│   │   ├── test_login.py
│   │   ├── test_store_search.py
│   │   ├── test_store_registration.py
│   │   ├── test_store_location.py
│   │   └── test_store_security.py
│   └── api/                        # API tests (Requests)
│       └── test_login_api.py
│
├── conftest.py                     # Global fixtures and hooks
├── pytest.ini                      # pytest config and markers
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.example                    # Example environment variables
└── README.md
```

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/HtestIs/mPointShop-Rework.git
cd mPointShop-Rework
```

### 2. Create and activate a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv venv

# Windows
venv\Scripts\activate

# macOS / Linux
source venv/bin/activate
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Configure environment

Copy the example file and fill in your values:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

```env
DEV_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api-url
DEV_WEB_BASE_URL=https://your-web-url
DEV_PARTNER_USERNAME=your_username
DEV_PARTNER_PASSWORD=your_password
DEV_MERCHANT_USERNAME=your_username
DEV_MERCHANT_PASSWORD=your_password
DEV_DUP_USERNAME=existing_username
```

> ⚠️ `.env` is not committed. Credentials are never hardcoded.

---

## ▶️ Running Tests

```bash
# Run all tests
pytest

# Run UI tests only
pytest tests/e2e

# Run API tests only
pytest tests/api

# Run by environment
pytest --env=dev
pytest --env=staging

# Run by marker
pytest -m smoke
pytest -m regression
pytest -m api

# Run in parallel
pytest -n 4

# Run with Allure report
pytest --alluredir=allure-results
allure serve allure-results
```

---

## 🏷️ Test Markers

| Marker | Description |
|---|---|
| `search` | Store search functionality |
| `registration` | Store creation and validation |
| `security` | Password and account lock scenarios |
| `api` | API tests |
| `smoke` | Critical path — run before every release |
| `regression` | Full test suite |
| `slow` | Long-running tests |

---

## ✨ Key Features

**Page Object Model (POM)**
Separates UI interaction logic from test logic — pages, fixtures, data, and utilities are fully decoupled.

**Data-driven Testing**
Uses `pytest.mark.parametrize` to cover validation scenarios, edge cases, and multi-field inputs cleanly.

**Environment-based Configuration**
UI base URL, API base URL, and credentials are managed through `.env` and `env_config.py` — switchable via `--env` CLI flag.

**Stable Synchronization**
Implements result-based waiting instead of `time.sleep()` to reduce flaky tests on dynamic UI elements.

**API Testing**
Login API tests cover success and failure scenarios, validating both HTTP status codes and business logic (response code, message body).

**Automatic Failure Artifacts**
On every test failure, Allure captures:
- 📸 Screenshot
- 🌐 Current URL
- 📄 Page source (HTML)
- 🖥️ Browser console logs

